From: WTA301 migration <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mount_root: honor fstools_overlay_name in `done` too

`start()` reads `fstools_overlay_name` from /proc/cmdline to pick the overlay
volume, but `done()` still looks up the hardcoded name "rootfs_data".  On a
board whose overlay volume is named differently (we use "wta301data" because
the mtdsplit `rootfs_data` partition would otherwise be picked up by the
rootdisk driver), `done()` gets NULL, returns early and never runs
fs_state_set("/overlay", FS_STATE_READY).

Consequence: /overlay/.fs_state stays absent, so every following boot takes the
FS_STATE_UNKNOWN -> FS_STATE_PENDING path in mount_overlay() and calls
overlay_delete(), i.e. it WIPES the whole overlay and reformats it.  Nothing a
user changes ever survives a reboot, silently.

dmesg shows it every boot:
    mount_root: overlay filesystem has not been fully initialized yet
    mount_root: switching to ubifs overlay

Fix: use the same lookup as `start`().

--- a/mount_root.c
+++ b/mount_root.c
@@ -115,7 +115,14 @@
 static int
 done(int argc, char *argv[1])
 {
-	struct volume *v = volume_find("rootfs_data");
+	char dataparam[BUFLEN];
+	char *dataname = "rootfs_data";
+	struct volume *v;
+
+	if (get_var_from_file("/proc/cmdline", "fstools_overlay_name", dataparam, sizeof(dataparam)))
+		dataname = dataparam;
+
+	v = volume_find(dataname);
 
 	if (!v)
 		return -1;
